Why Is Demand Increasing
Cardiovascular Disease Burden — Increasing prevalence of myocardial infarction, heart failure, and other cardiovascular conditions is creating continued demand for rapid biomarker-based diagnosis.
Point-of-Care Testing — Rapid tests allow cardiac biomarkers to be evaluated closer to the patient, supporting faster triage and clinical decision-making in time-sensitive situations.
Multiparameter Diagnostics — Manufacturers are developing tests capable of detecting multiple biomarkers, including troponin, CK-MB, and myoglobin, broadening diagnostic utility.

Clinical & Diagnostic Watch: Faster Cardiac Assessment Gains Importance
Cardiac marker testing is increasingly integrated into emergency departments, clinics, ambulatory settings, and decentralized diagnostic environments. Advances in lateral-flow immunoassay technology are improving the speed and utility of rapid testing, while high-sensitivity biomarker detection continues to influence the development of next-generation cardiac diagnostic solutions.

